@param Circ source circle
@param Dist signed distance
@remarks **Note:** If `Dist` is positive, the result encloses `Circ`.
@remarks **Note:** If `Dist` is negative, the result is enclosed by `Circ`.

Creates a circle coaxial to input circle and passing through a point.
@param Circ source circle
@param Point reference point

Creates a circle from axis and radius.
@param Axis axis definition
@param Radius radius value
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `Radius` is negative.

Creates a circle passing through three points.
@param P1 first point
@param P2 second point
@param P3 third point

Creates a circle from center, plane normal and radius.
@param Center center point
@param Norm input value
@param Radius radius value

Creates a circle from center, reference plane and radius.
@param Center center point
@param Plane reference plane
@param Radius radius value

Creates a circle from center, axis-defining point and radius.
@param Center center point
@param Ptaxis point defining axis direction
@param Radius radius value

