classes.summary:
This class implements construction algorithms for `gp_Cone`. Supported constructions include:
- from axis placement, semi-angle and reference radius;
- cone coaxial to another cone, through a point or at signed offset;
- cone from four points;
- cone from axis and two points;
- cone from two axis points and two section radii.

constructors.comment:
Creates a cone coaxial to input cone and passing through a point.
@param Cone source cone
@param Point reference point
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` when no non-negative solution radius can be found.

Creates a cone coaxial to input cone at signed distance.
@param Cone source cone
@param Dist signed distance
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NullAngle` if semi-angle cosine is numerically too small.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if resulting radius is negative.

Creates a cone from axis placement, semi-angle and reference radius.
@param A2 local coordinate system
@param Ang angle value
@param Radius radius value
@remarks **Note:** `A2` defines cone position and reference section plane.
@remarks **Note:** `Ang` is the cone semi-angle (radians), expected in ]0, PI/2[.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `Radius` is negative.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_BadAngle` if `Ang <= gp::Resolution()` or `PI/2 - Ang <= gp::Resolution()`.

Creates a cone from line axis and two points.
@param Axis axis definition
@param P1 first point
@param P2 second point
@remarks **Note:** Distance from `P1` to axis gives first section radius.
@remarks **Note:** Distance from `P2` to axis gives second section radius.
@remarks **Note:** Error status is propagated from the 4-point construction.

Creates a cone from line axis and two points.
@param Axis axis definition
@param P1 first point
@param P2 second point
@remarks **Note:** Distance from `P1` to axis gives first section radius.
@remarks **Note:** Distance from `P2` to axis gives second section radius.
@remarks **Note:** Error status is propagated from the 4-point construction.

Creates a cone from four points.
@param P1 first point
@param P2 second point
@param P3 third point
@param P4 fourth point
@remarks **Note:** `P1` and `P2` define the axis direction.
@remarks **Note:** Distance from `P3` to that axis defines base radius.
@remarks **Note:** Distance from `P4` to that axis defines radius of section through `P4`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_ConfusedPoints` if `P1`/`P2` or `P3`/`P4` are coincident.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NullAngle` if section distances produce zero cone angle.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NullRadius` for degenerate right-angle or zero-angle radius configuration.

Creates a cone from two axis points and two section radii.
@param P1 first point
@param P2 second point
@param R1 first radius value
@param R2 second radius value
@remarks **Note:** The axis is the line passing through `P1` and `P2`.
@remarks **Note:** `R1` is section radius at `P1`, `R2` is section radius at `P2`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NullAxis` if `P1` and `P2` are coincident.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `R1` or `R2` is negative.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NullAngle` for degenerate zero-angle or right-angle configurations.

classes.summary:
