classes.summary:
This class implements construction algorithms for `gp_Elips`. Supported constructions include:
- ellipse from local coordinate system and radii;
- ellipse from center and two points.

constructors.comment:
The major radius of the ellipse is on the "XAxis" and the minor radius is on the "YAxis" of the ellipse. The "XAxis" is defined with the "XDirection" of A2 and the "YAxis" is defined with the "YDirection" of A2.
@param A2 local coordinate system
@param MajorRadius major radius value
@param MinorRadius minor radius value
@remarks **Note:** It is possible to create an ellipse with `MajorRadius == MinorRadius`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_InvertRadius` if `MajorRadius < MinorRadius`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `MinorRadius < 0.0`.

Creates an ellipse from center and two points.
@param S1 first point
@param S2 second point
@param Center center point
@remarks **Note:** `S1` defines major radius direction and value.
@remarks **Note:** Minor radius is computed as distance from `S2` to major axis.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NullAxis` if `S1` and `Center` coincide.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_InvertAxis` when computed minor radius is null/greater than major radius, or when points are collinear.

classes.summary:
This class implements construction algorithms for `gp_Elips2d`. Supported constructions include:
- ellipse from major axis (or local 2D coordinate system) and radii;
- ellipse from center and two points.

constructors.comment:
Axis defines the Xaxis and Yaxis of the ellipse which defines the origin and the sense of parametrization. Creates an ellipse with the AxisPlacement the major and the minor radius. The location of Axis is the center of the ellipse. It is possible to create an ellipse with MajorRadius = MinorRadius.
@param A local coordinate system
@param MajorRadius major radius value
@param MinorRadius minor radius value
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_InvertRadius` if `MajorRadius < MinorRadius`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `MajorRadius < 0.0`.

Creates an ellipse from center and two points.
@param S1 first point
@param S2 second point
@param Center center point
@remarks **Note:** `S1` defines major radius direction and value.
@remarks **Note:** Minor radius is computed as distance from `S2` to major axis.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NullAxis` when computed minor radius is null.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_InvertAxis` when computed minor radius exceeds major radius.

Creates an ellipse with the major axis, the major and the minor radius. The location of the MajorAxis is the center of the ellipse. The sense of parametrization is given by Sense. It is possible to create an ellipse with MajorRadius = MinorRadius.
@param MajorAxis major axis placement
@param MajorRadius major radius value
@param MinorRadius minor radius value
@param Sense orientation flag
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_InvertRadius` if `MajorRadius < MinorRadius`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `MajorRadius < 0.0`.

Creates a hyperbola from a local coordinate system and radii.
@param A2 local coordinate system
@param MajorRadius major radius value
@param MinorRadius minor radius value
@remarks **Note:** In the local coordinate system of `A2`, the equation is `X*X / (MajorRadius*MajorRadius) - Y*Y / (MinorRadius*MinorRadius) = 1.0`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction with `MajorRadius == MinorRadius` is valid.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `MajorRadius < 0.0` or `MinorRadius < 0.0`.

Creates a hyperbola from center and two points.
@param S1 first point
@param S2 second point
@param Center center point
@remarks **Note:** `Center` is the hyperbola center, `Center`-`S1` defines the major axis, major radius is `Distance(Center, S1)`, and minor radius is distance from `S2` to this major axis.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_ConfusedPoints` if any two of `S1`, `S2`, and `Center` are coincident.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_ColinearPoints` if `S1`, `S2`, and `Center` are collinear.

Creates a hyperbola from center and two points.
@param S1 first point
@param S2 second point
@param Center center point
@remarks **Note:** `Center` is the hyperbola center, `Center`-`S1` defines major axis, major radius is `Distance(Center, S1)`, and minor radius is distance from `S2` to this major axis.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_ConfusedPoints` if any two of `S1`, `S2`, and `Center` are coincident.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_ColinearPoints` if `S1`, `S2`, and `Center` are collinear.

Creates a hyperbola from local coordinate system and radii.
@param A local coordinate system
@param MajorRadius major radius value
@param MinorRadius minor radius value
@remarks **Note:** The result is centered at `A.Location()`, and its major axis follows the X axis direction of `A`.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `MajorRadius < 0.0` or `MinorRadius < 0.0`.

Creates a hyperbola from major axis and radii.
@param MajorAxis major axis placement
@param MajorRadius major radius value
@param MinorRadius minor radius value
@param Sense orientation flag
@remarks **Note:** Center is located at `MajorAxis.Location()`.
@remarks **Note:** If `Sense` is `false`, the opposite direction of `MajorAxis` is used.
@remarks **Note:** Construction fails with `gce_NegativeRadius` if `MajorRadius < 0.0` or `MinorRadius < 0.0`.

